GLORB Running spatial phase correction -- virtual acceptance record
Date: 2026-11-14
Base: tycwled b3b6229
Status: short regression and both 4201-frame SR-off/SR-on comparisons passed

Change
  Running advances the spatial phase before sampling the first pixel.
  Only i * x_scale becomes (i + 1) * x_scale; persistent step and hue state
  remain the base phases. No other effect, palette, gamma or configuration changes.

Original mechanism
  Supported GLORB.1.3 debug ESP32-S3 application SHA256:
  888454572bc34beb86e1595e86aef3ff9f477e2f6501201011e91279f29c597a
  dis_running.txt: 0x42043472 copies the base phase into a7;
  0x42043474 initializes pixel index zero; 0x4204348f adds x_scale;
  0x42043494 selects the low eight bits; 0x42043497 calls original sin8.
  Thus the first sample already includes one spatial increment.
  This supersedes NOTES.md's previous ap + i*x_scale and exactness claims
  for Running. The error is spatial; the persisted segment state already matched.

