Actual candidate WLED virtual bus
  The fixed fleet_glorb application boots on virtual ESP32-S3 and executes its
  genuine JSON parser and serializer. The bounded solid-color test captures
  one startup transfer and seven normal 360-byte GRB transfers: all 80 mapped
  LEDs equal [32,16,64], and the 40 unused physical positions remain black.
  All three loaded executable/read-only segments match the image before and
  after capture. An actual driver-buffer mutation changes byte3 of capture1
  from32 to33; the ordinary comparator rejects that exact one-byte difference.
  Eighteen corruption controls pass. An independent verification also passes.
  USB CDC availability/input/output and ADC calibration are declared API/SDK
  substitutions; AudioReactive is disabled only in the disposable configuration.
  This is an instrumented diagnostic profile, not as-shipped runtime acceptance.
  This verifies candidate boot/mapping/output access, not original/candidate
  scene equivalence, microphone DSP, long stability or physical output.

Long execution
  Two sequential Running cases, SR off/on, each 4201 actual frames
  through 100.000 scripted seconds, 42Hz rounded to millisecond frame times.
  Each original execution is bounded to 90 minutes; the detached service has
  one shared emulator slot, 3GiB memory and no swap. It started with one CPU of
  quota. At 03:43:23 UTC the quota was raised to two CPUs after 34.2 seconds of
  cgroup throttling in 519 seconds; 420 frames had been observed. The original
  launcher record is retained and a separate timestamped resource-event log
  records both limits and the successful change. Frame count, input, timeout
  and firmware pins were unchanged; the same single JVM continued running.
  Two early preflight failures are retained separately (redundant post-launcher
  HOLD flag; sub-millisecond timestamps unsupported by the adapter). Neither
  started Java or executed firmware. The fully preflighted run is attempt v3.

